":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2023-01-30T04:31:03Z","updated_at":"2023-01-31T22:08:26Z","closed_at":"2023-01-31T22:08:25Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Describe the typing issue\r\n\r\nAccording to the [`GenerativeSelect.limit`](https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/20/core/selectable.html#sqlalchemy.sql.expression.GenerativeSelect.limit.params.limit) and [`GenerativeSelect.offset`](https://docs.sqlalchemy.org/en/20/core/selectable.html#sqlalchemy.sql.expression.GenerativeSelect.offset.params.offset) docs, `None` can be passed to reset limit / option.\r\n\r\nHowever the type checker doesn't allow those parameters to be `None`.\r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Select, select\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Base(DeclarativeBase):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Table(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"table\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef query_limit() -> Select[tuple[Table]]:\r\n    return select(\r\n        Table,\r\n    ).limit(None)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef query_offset() -> Select[tuple[Table]]:\r\n    return select(\r\n        Table,\r\n    ).offset(None)\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Error\r\n\r\n```\r\ntestcase.py:16: error: Argument 1 to \"limit\" of \"GenerativeSelect\" has incompatible type \"None\"; expected \"Union[int, _HasClauseElement, SQLCoreOperations[int], ExpressionElementRole[int], Callable[[], ColumnElement[int]], LambdaElement]\"  [arg-type]\r\ntestcase.py:22: error: Argument 1 to \"offset\" of \"GenerativeSelect\" has incompatible type \"None\"; expected \"Union[int, _HasClauseElement, SQLCoreOperations[int], ExpressionElementRole[int], Callable[[], ColumnElement[int]], LambdaElement]\"  [arg-type]\r\n``` \r\n\r\n### Versions\r\n\r\n- OS: Linux Mint 21.1 Vera\r\n- Python: 3.11\r\n- SQLAlchemy: 2.0.0\r\n- Type checker (eg: mypy 0.991, pyright 1.1.290, etc): mypy 0.991\r\n\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9183/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/9183/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}